WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.172
Partitions are central to Spark parallelism.

00:00:03.172 --> 00:00:08.557
A dataset is divided into pieces, and tasks process those pieces.

00:00:08.557 --> 00:00:11.952
Too few partitions can limit parallelism.

00:00:11.952 --> 00:00:15.497
Too many small partitions can create overhead.

00:00:15.497 --> 00:00:19.462
As a beginner, you do not need to tune every partition setting,

00:00:19.462 --> 00:00:23.237
but you should understand why partitioning affects performance.

00:00:23.237 --> 00:00:29.432
Partitions organize data so the engine can avoid reading files that cannot satisfy a filter.

00:00:29.432 --> 00:00:34.782
Good partition columns are commonly filtered and have manageable cardinality.

00:00:34.782 --> 00:00:38.622
Column pruning similarly avoids reading unused columns.

00:00:38.622 --> 00:00:43.254
Both optimizations reduce I/O before more expensive computation begins.
